# rpmlint filters for sofka. Everything here is inherent to repackaging
# upstream's prebuilt, stripped Rust release binary rather than compiling
# from source, or a deliberate packaging choice.

# Upstream ships the binary already stripped; there is no separate debug
# info to extract, and no testsuite to run in the build root either.
addFilter(r"no-%check-section")

# Source0/1 are bare filenames, not URLs - see the comment in _service and
# in the README ("Kept as bare filenames so OBS does not treat them as
# stored blobs"). rpmlint's invalid-url check doesn't know about scmsync
# source services.
addFilter(r"invalid-url Source[01]:")

# Spell-checker false positives: upstream's own tagline and library/
# ecosystem names (kube-rs, ratatui), plus our own target distro - none of
# which are in the dictionary rpmlint's Enchant backend uses.
addFilter(r"spelling-error \('(reimagined|kube|ratatui|openSUSE)'")
